OPTIONS
=======

Everything you can set in Odin: its files, the command line, the file
odin.ini and the environment variables. The menu (Escape, F10 or Guide)
sets most of it too and writes the changes to odin.ini for you.


FILES
-----

Odin keeps its files in one folder:
 Linux     ~/.local/share/odin  (or $XDG_DATA_HOME/odin)
 Windows   %APPDATA%\odin
 macOS     ~/Library/Application Support/odin
 Portable  beside the program: put an empty portable.txt (or odin.ini)
           there, and Odin keeps everything in that folder.

In it:
 odin.ini                 The settings.
 odin.log                 What Odin says, rewritten at each start
                          (odin-previous.log: the one before); its folder
                          can be changed ([paths] log).
 saves/<game>/            What the board keeps without power: mie_eeprom,
                          nvram, main_eeprom, rombd_eeprom, clock, cards/.
 states/                  Saved states (<game>.odinstate).
 artwork/                 The pictures of the games, from
                          Odin-Artwork.zip or your own: <game>_title.png
                          (the library; a <game>_logo.png is shown
                          instead), <game>_bezel.png and
                          <game>_bezel.info (Batocera's format). A
                          version of a game uses its parent's pictures.

Elsewhere: the shader lists and the driver's programs, rebuilt when
missing (page Paths, Shader lists): cache/ beside a portable Odin, else
$XDG_CACHE_HOME/odin, else .cache/odin in the home folder.


COMMAND LINE
------------

 odin [options]

 -r <game>        Play this game (its MAME name: airtrix, braveff...).
                  Without -r, Odin opens its library.
 -R <folder>      Folder of the games (one folder, zip or 7z per game).
 -B <folder>      Folder of the shared sets (hikaru, mie; optional:
                  jvs13551, 18wheelr, srally2). Default: the folder of the
                  games.
 -c <file>        The settings file to use instead of odin.ini.
 -x <1 to 6>      Draw the 3D this many times finer than 640 x 480.
 -a <2 to 16>     Anisotropic filtering of the textures (the board has none).
 -w <n>           Window n times 640 x 480, as far as the display has
                  room.
 -f               Full screen (F11 or Alt+Enter switches).
 -o <mode>        Sound: main, option, mix, quad or off (see [sound.<game>]).
 -u               No speed limit (faster than 60 frames per second), no
                  sound.
 -l <file>        Load a saved state at start.
 -s <n>[,<n>...]  Save <game>-<nnnnnn>.odinstate (the frame on six
                  digits) in the current folder after these frames.
 -n <n>           Stop after frame n.
 -v               Detailed log of the board (slow).
 -V, --version    Show the version (e.g. Odin v0.1.1) and exit.
 -h, --help       Show the help.

The command line comes before odin.ini.


ODIN.INI
--------

Where it is: in Odin's folder (see FILES above), or the file given by
-c <file> or ODIN_CONFIG=<file>.

Odin writes every setting it knows. A line that starts with # is at its
default value: remove the # and change the value. A wrong line is ignored
and said in the log.

Values: on/off, numbers, names, folders. An input list is several inputs
apart by commas (see INPUTS below).


[display]

 scale         1 to 6          3D resolution, times 640 x 480. Default 1.
 upscale_mode  raw, snap,      How flat 2D pieces (HUD, text) are drawn
               native          above scale 1. raw: fine like the rest;
                               snap: corners on the board's pixels;
                               native: as on the board. Default raw.
 anisotropy    1 to 16         Texture filtering. Default 1 (none).
 window        1 to 6, or      Window size: times 640 x 480, or a size.
               <w>x<h>         Default 1.
 fullscreen    on, off         Default off.
 vsync         off, on,        Wait for the display. adaptive: a late
               adaptive        frame does not wait. Default off.
 unthrottled   on, off         No speed limit, no sound. Default off.
 show_speed    on, off         Frames per second in the title. Default on.
 api           opengl, vulkan  What draws, from the next start.
                               Default vulkan on macOS, opengl elsewhere.
 gpu           a card name     The card Vulkan draws on, as page Display
                               names it ("... (2)" for a second of a
                               kind). Default empty: the best one.
 bezel        off, blur,      Around the game: black, its blurred edges,
               image           or its bezel picture (black without
                               one). Default image.
 filter        none, or a      CRT filter (page Display, CRT screen).
               filter name     Default none. The screens of the
                               cabinets:
                                 lola-retro/sega-monitor-29
                                 lola-retro/sega-projector-50
                                 lola-retro/gaelco-monitor-28
                                 lola-retro/gaelco-monitor-34

[sound]

 device        a device name   The sound device (page Audio lists them).
                               Default: the system's.
 volume        0 to 100        Default 100.
 background    on, off         Sound when the window is in the background.
                               Default on.

[menu]

 theme         runasteinn,     Colours of the menu, bar and library.
               edda, raf,      Default runasteinn.
               heimdall
 classic       on, off         Page Input as a list. Default off.
 animations    on, off         Default on.

