                               linked to other Odins. Default none.
 port          a port          Where the cabinet before connects.
                               Default 13404.
 next          address[:port]  The cabinet after. Empty: this one.
 cabinet       1 to 8          Which cabinet this is. 1 is the master.
                               Default 1.


PER GAME
--------

<game> is the MAME name: airtrix, braveff, pharrier, sgnascar, swracer,
von4; atvtrack, gfootbal, smashdrv. A version of a game (airtrixo,
sgnascaro, atvtracka, smashdrvb, smashdrvs) shares the sections of its
parent; the lines of a section of its own (an older Odin wrote one) still
count, after its parent's.

[players.<game>]

 p1, p2           <GUID> <name>   Gamepad of player 1, 2.
 joy1, joy2       <GUID> <name>   Wheel or other joystick of player 1, 2
                                  (a wheel: NASCAR, ATV Track, Smashing
                                  Drive, one player).
 p1_path,         <path>          The very gamepad of player 1, 2 when two
 p2_path,                         alike share a GUID: its path, as the log
 joy1_path,                       names it ("pad: ... plugged, <GUID> at
 joy2_path                        <path>"); on Linux, for a path
                                  /dev/input/event..., a link to it of
                                  /dev/input/by-path or by-id too. The
                                  page Input and the bar write it when two
                                  alike are plugged in. Gone or changed: any
                                  of the GUID asked. On Windows an Xbox pad is
                                  XInput#0 to #3; the SDL 2 of a frontend
                                  (before 2.33) names it by its raw input
                                  path, as Odin does when started with
                                  SDL_JOYSTICK_RAWINPUT=1.
 device1,         keyboard, pad,  What the player plays with (it alone
 device2          joystick        shakes or turns). Default: Odin picks.
 gun1, gun2       <identity>      Light gun of player 1, 2, as the log
                  <name>          names it ("pointer: ..."), e.g.
                                  "vidpid:1209:0001 GUN4IR".
 hide_cursor      on, off         No cursor, no bar: the mouse controls
                                  the game (off: a normal pointer).
                                  Default on when a control of player 1
                                  or of the cabinet (coin, test...) uses
                                  the mouse (the sight of braveff), else
                                  off. light_gun_mode before 0.1.1.
 sinden_border    on, off         White border for a Sinden gun.
                                  Default off.
 sinden_border_   game, window    Border around the game (4:3) or the
 style                            whole window. Default game.
 sinden_border_   2 to 30         Border width in pixels. Default 2.
 size
 vibration        on, off         The device shakes with the game.
                                  Default on.
 vibration_force  0 to 200        Shake strength, in %. Default 100.
 wheel_force      0 to 200        Force feedback strength, in % (NASCAR,
                                  ATV Track, Smashing Drive). Default 100.
 wheel_rotation   0, 270, 360,    How far the wheel turns from one end to
                  540, 900, 1080  the other (0: all the way). Default 0.
 invert           <id>, ...       Controls turned the other way, on every
                                  device: pharrier stick_v (push up to
                                  climb; the cabinet's stick climbs pulled
                                  back). Default none.
 cabinet          standard,       The cabinet model: deluxe (NASCAR),
                  deluxe,         minideluxe (Star Wars Racer), vibrator
                  minideluxe,     (ATV Track: Odin sets its MOTION SYSTEM
                  vibrator,       to VIBRATOR; on another cabinet, a
                  upright         VIBRATOR goes back to PLATFORM HARD),
                                  upright (Smashing Drive). Default
                                  standard.
 card             <name>          Virtual-On card in hand (von4).

[sound.<game>]

 Games with a second sound board: pharrier, sgnascar, swracer.

 mode             main, mix, quad  main: main board only. mix: both on two
                                   speakers. quad: four channels.
                                   Default mix (swracer: main).
 option_level     -60 to 12       Level of the second board, in dB.
                                  Default 0 (NASCAR -12, swracer -13).

 Games with a woofer: the Gaelco games (atvtrack, gfootbal, smashdrv).

 mode             main, mix, quad  main: left and right only. mix: the
                                   woofer's lows in both. quad: left,
                                   right, woofer and the board's fourth
                                   channel. Default mix. With -o option:
                                   the woofer's channel alone.
 woofer_level     -60 to 12       Level of the woofer in the mix, in dB.
                                  Default 0.
 woofer_cutoff    80, 120, 160,   The woofer's lows below that many Hz in
