INPUTS
------

 key:<name>          A key, by SDL's name: key:A, key:Left Ctrl, key:Space.
 pad:<button>        A gamepad button, by SDL's name: a, b, x, y, back,
                     guide, start, leftstick, rightstick, leftshoulder,
                     rightshoulder, dpup, dpdown, dpleft, dpright, misc1
                     to misc6, paddle1 to paddle4, touchpad.
 pad:<axis>          A whole axis: leftx, lefty, rightx, righty,
                     lefttrigger, righttrigger.
 pad:-<axis>         Half an axis: pad:-lefty is the left stick up,
 pad:+<axis>         pad:+leftx the left stick right.
 pad:<axis>:invert   A whole stick axis turned over (not a trigger).
 pad:<a>+<b>         Button b while a is held: pad:guide+x, pad:back+start
                     (what the hotkey button holds for a shortcut is not
                     seen by the game; Guide, all it holds).
 joy:axis<n>         An axis of a wheel or joystick; joy:-axis<n> and
                     joy:+axis<n> its halves; joy:axis<n>:invert turned
                     over. A pedal goes away from where it rests, as
                     written or not; :invert only picks the half of an
                     axis two pedals share.
 joy:button<n>       A button of a wheel or joystick.
 joy:hat<n>_up       A hat direction (_up, _down, _left, _right).
 joy:gas             The gas pedal of a known wheel, whatever its numbers
                     (Logitech G25 to G923, PRO, Driving Force, MOMO;
                     Thrustmaster FFB Wheel, T150, T300, Advance Racer;
                     MOZA R12); nothing on another joystick. joy:brake,
                     joy:paddle_left, joy:paddle_right, joy:start and
                     joy:select the same. On a button, a pedal presses it
                     from half its way.
 joy@<GUID>:<input>  The same on another joystick than the player's (a
                     shifter or pedals of their own), by its GUID as the
                     log names it, e.g.
                     joy@030000006d0400001ac2000000000000:button1. The
                     page Input writes it when it catches such a joystick.
 mouse:left          Mouse or light gun buttons: left, middle, right, side,
                     extra.
 mouse:x, mouse:y    Where the mouse or the light gun aims.

The log names each joystick when it is plugged in, with how many axes,
buttons and hats it has (numbered from 0).


ENVIRONMENT
-----------

For players:

 ODIN_CONFIG=<file>         Read another odin.ini (before -c); none: no
                            settings file.
 ODIN_SAVES=<folder>        Another saves folder; none: keep nothing.
 ODIN_ARTWORK=<folder>      Another artwork folder; none: no pictures.
 ODIN_LOG=<file>            Another log file (before [paths] log);
                            none: no log file.
 ODIN_CONTROLLERS=none      No gamepads, joysticks, mouse or light guns.
 ODIN_STOP_BOX=0            No error box when the board stops (for a
                            frontend).
 ODIN_DRIVE=imitation       NASCAR's drive board imitated, not run.
 ODIN_IO=imitation          The I/O board imitated, not run.
 ODIN_CARD_FILE=<file>      The Virtual-On card in hand.
 ODIN_MIE_EEPROM=<file>     Keep the cabinet settings (MIE EEPROM) elsewhere.
 ODIN_CLOCK_FILE=<file>     Keep the board's clock elsewhere.
 SDL_JOYSTICK_HIDAPI_LG4FF=1  Use SDL's own driver for Logitech wheels
                            (it turns their centring spring off).

For developers (tests and debugging):

 ODIN_SCREENSHOT=<prefix>   <prefix>-<frame>.ppm every 60 frames
 ODIN_SCREENSHOT_EVERY=<n>  ... or every n frames.
 ODIN_WINDOW_SHOT=<prefix>  The whole window, to <prefix>-<what>-<frame>.ppm.
 ODIN_PICTURE_FP=1          A fingerprint of each picture on stderr.
 ODIN_WINDOW_FP=1           The same for the whole window.
 ODIN_LIST_FP=1             A fingerprint of each display list.
 ODIN_LIST_DUMP=<n>         ... with a line for each mesh of frame n.
 ODIN_LISTS_TEST=1          No room for translucent pieces at first (a
                            test of the lists).
 ODIN_SPEED=1               Frames per second every 60 frames, on stderr.
 ODIN_STATS=1               Drawing and waiting times at the end.
 ODIN_DRAW_TIMES=1          The cost of each part of a frame's drawing.
 ODIN_LATE_DRAW=1           Draw a frame after the board ran the next one.
 ODIN_DEBUG_KEYS=1          Keys that switch 2D layers, 3D, textures,
                            lighting... (see renderer_debug.cpp).
 HR_LOG=1, HR_LOG_FRAME=<n> Log of what is drawn (every frame, or one).
 GPU_LOG_CP=1, GPU_LOG_DMA=1, GPU_LOG_IDMA=1
                            Log of the GPU's commands and transfers.
 ODIN_VK_VALIDATION=1       Vulkan validation layers.
 ODIN_DUMPS=1               Each memory to <game>-<memory>.bin at the end.
 ODIN_WAV=<file>            The sound to a WAV file.
 ODIN_LOG_REPEATS=1         Every repeated log line (not only the first).
 ODIN_SH4_MHZ=<n>           A slower SH-4 clock (faster tests).
 ODIN_SH4_NO_FMA=1          The SH-4 path of hosts without FMA.
 ODIN_SH4_TRANSLATE=0       The SH-4 interpreted, not translated.
 ODIN_SH4_TRACE=<prefix>    A trace of the SH-4s, a line per slice.
 ODIN_ARM7_TRANSLATE=0      The ARM7 interpreted, not translated.
 ODIN_PMX1_TRANSLATE=0      The Neon 250's blocks run from their decoded ops.
 ODIN_ARM7_DECODED=0        The ARM7 decodes every instruction.
 ODIN_ARM7_TRACE=<prefix>   A trace of the ARM7s.
 ODIN_TURNS=0               Waiting loops run, not counted.
 ODIN_MIE_TRACE=<file>      A trace of the MIE's Z80
 ODIN_MIE_TRACE_N=<n>       ... for n instructions (300000)
